#import(../prelude/rat.ill)

% PP2 — the till settlement demo (TODO_0011 acceptance: rung-1 sorts +
% the §3 numeric collapse, all in one small game).
%
% Everything the shell displays is knowledge in the logic:
%   - tokens are classified by CLASSIFIER SORTS (`wood: resource.`) — the
%     shell groups stock rows by membership, %#display is gone
%   - the spoilage law is ONE classifier schema over per-member DATA:
%     `shelf r D` facts give each resource its shelf life, and the window
%     `after (Q + D)` lowers onto the SHARED `plus` (bin instance for the
%     integers here, /q instance if a shelf life were ever fractional —
%     same predicate, dispatched by matching)
%   - every delay/count is sort-checked: shelf lives sit at (d: delay),
%     grade sorts delay/count/weight <: q join the numeric tower in rat.ill
%
% Play:  npm run shell:till -- calculus/till/game/PP2.till --init play
%   digits buy from the standing build menu. Stock rots when its shelf
%   life runs out — food fast, wood slowly; farms and quarries keep fresh
%   stock coming.

resource: sort.
wood: resource.
stone: resource.
food: resource.

camp: type.
farm: type.
quarry: type.

% production loops ($ = preserved building)
grow: $farm -o { food }@4.
mine: $quarry -o { stone }@6.

% forage: the camp gathers wood, slowly
forage: $camp -o { wood }@9.

% per-resource shelf life — data, not rules
shelf: (r: resource) -> (d: delay) -> type.
shelf/wood: shelf wood 60.
shelf/stone: shelf stone 120.
shelf/food: shelf food 10.

% perishability — ONE schema, one rule per resource after expansion; the
% deadline Q + D goes through the shared numeric plus
spoil: (r: resource) r@Q * !shelf r D * after (Q + D) -o { I }.

% standing build menu: wood buys a farm, stone buys a quarry.
% `!_3 wood` takes 3 wood of ANY ages (D4 revised: an unstamped count
% binds no stamp, so it spreads across cohorts oldest-first — the form
% `!_3 wood@T` would demand one same-stamp batch instead).
#play (settle: 0)
  camp
  * !(( !_3 wood -o { farm }@5 ) & ( !_2 stone -o { quarry }@8 ))
  * !_3 wood * !_2 stone * food
  =>
  camp .
